-- CK-03: a method used on a receiver that is already on a cycle is ONE
-- `infinite_type` at the use, the cycle poisoned, and no method looked up on
-- its head (checker-v2.md §9.5, as built by R6a's review, F5): `x` is
-- `Maybe x` once `[ x, Just x ]` is solved, before `x.foo ()` and `x == x`.
-- On 68186fa v1 reports the cycle at the body and also `unknown_method`
-- (`Maybe` has no `foo`), the cycle's consequence. Known two-message case
-- (round-2 review, nit 1): with the method FIRST, `( x.foo (), x == Just x )`,
-- the wanted is resolved on `Maybe a'` before the cycle closes, so its
-- `unknown_method` is honest then and both checkers give both messages.
n x =
    ( [ x, Just x ], x.foo () )


m x =
    ( [ x, Just x ], x == x )
